  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nThe ``TrailsIntentEntrypoint contract`` is designed to work with Sequence v3 wallets (smart contract wallets) but uses ECDSA.recover() for signature validation, which only works with EOA (Externally Owned Account) signatures. This makes the contract completely incompatible with its intended user base - smart contract wallets.\n\n## Root Cause\n```solidity\naddress recovered = ECDSA.recover(digest, sigV, sigR, sigS);\nif (recovered != user) revert InvalidIntentSignature();\n```\nThis fails when user is a smart contract wallet (like Sequence), because:\n- The signature is produced by the wallet owner (EOA).\n- ECDSA.recover() returns the owner, not the wallet address.\n- recovered != user → revert.\n\nSmart wallets require EIP-1271 (isValidSignature) to validate signatures.\n\n\n## Impact\nThe contract is completely unusable by its intended primary user base as stated in the doc: Sequence v3 wallets.\n- Users with smart wallets cannot deposit via intents.\n- All off-chain signed intents fail on-chain.\n- The core value proposition (\"deposit to intent addresses with signed intents\") fails silently.\n- Users may lose gas and believe the system is broken.\n\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nImplement EIP-1271 fallback in signature verification:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _verifySignature(\n    address user,\n    bytes32 digest,\n    uint8 v,\n    bytes32 r,\n    bytes32 s\n) internal view returns (bool) {\n    // Try ECDSA recovery first (for EOAs)\n    address signer = ECDSA.recover(digest, v, r, s);\n    if (signer == user) return true;\n\n    // Fallback to EIP-1271 for smart wallets\n    if (Address.isContract(user)) {\n        bytes memory sig = abi.encodePacked(r, s, v);\n        return IERC1271(user).isValidSignature(digest, sig) == 0x1626ba7e;\n    }\n\n    return false;\n}\n```\nThen use:\n```solidity\nif (!_verifySignature(user, digest, v, r, s)) revert InvalidIntentSignature();```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Create a test file and past the following test and run with,\n forge test --match-test test_POC_SmartWalletSignatureAlwaysFails\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport {Test, console} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {TrailsIntentEntrypoint} from \"../src/TrailsIntentEntrypoint.sol\";\nimport {ERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Permit} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/extensions/ERC20Permit.sol\";\nimport {IERC1271} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC1271.sol\";\n\n// Mock ERC20 token with permit functionality\ncontract MockERC20Permit is ERC20, ERC20Permit {\n    constructor() ERC20(\"Mock Token\", \"MTK\") ERC20Permit(\"Mock Token\") {\n        _mint(msg.sender, 1000000 * 10 ** decimals());\n    }\n}\n\n// Mock Sequence-like Smart Contract Wallet that implements EIP-1271\ncontract MockSequenceWallet is IERC1271 {\n    address public owner;\n    \n    constructor(address _owner) {\n        owner = _owner;\n    }\n    \n    // EIP-1271 signature validation\n    function isValidSignature(bytes32 hash, bytes memory signature) \n        external \n        view \n        override \n        returns (bytes4 magicValue) \n    {\n        // Extract v, r, s from signature\n        require(signature.length == 65, \"Invalid signature length\");\n        \n        bytes32 r;\n        bytes32 s;\n        uint8 v;\n        \n        assembly {\n            r := mload(add(signature, 0x20))\n            s := mload(add(signature, 0x40))\n            v := byte(0, mload(add(signature, 0x60)))\n        }\n        \n        // Recover signer from signature\n        address signer = ecrecover(hash, v, r, s);\n        \n        // Check if signer is the owner\n        if (signer == owner) {\n            return 0x1626ba7e; // EIP-1271 magic value\n        } else {\n            return 0xffffffff; // Invalid signature\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Allow wallet to receive tokens\n    function executeCall(address target, bytes calldata data) external returns (bool, bytes memory) {\n        require(msg.sender == owner, \"Only owner\");\n        return target.call(data);\n    }\n}\n\n// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Test Contract - Demonstrates EIP-1271 Bug\n// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ncontract EIP1271BugPOC is Test {\n    TrailsIntentEntrypoint public entrypoint;\n    MockERC20Permit public token;\n    MockSequenceWallet public wallet;\n    \n    address public owner;\n    uint256 public ownerKey;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        // Setup owner\n        ownerKey = 0x123456789;\n        owner = vm.addr(ownerKey);\n        \n        // Deploy contracts\n        entrypoint = new TrailsIntentEntrypoint();\n        token = new MockERC20Permit();\n        wallet = new MockSequenceWallet(owner);\n        \n        // Give wallet tokens\n        token.transfer(address(wallet), 1000 * 10 ** token.decimals());\n        \n        // Wallet approves entrypoint\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        wallet.executeCall(\n            address(token),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(token.approve.selector, address(entrypoint), type(uint256).max)\n        );\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice POC: TrailsIntentEntrypoint ALWAYS FAILS with smart contract wallets\n    \n     */\n    function test_POC_SmartWalletSignatureAlwaysFails() public {\n        address intentAddr = address(0x5678);\n        uint256 amount = 50 * 10 ** token.decimals();\n        uint256 deadline = block.timestamp + 3600;\n        uint256 nonce = entrypoint.nonces(address(wallet));\n\n        // Create intent hash - signed by wallet OWNER\n        bytes32 intentHash = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                entrypoint.TRAILS_INTENT_TYPEHASH(),\n                address(wallet), // user = wallet contract address\n                address(token),\n                amount,\n                intentAddr,\n                deadline,\n                block.chainid,\n                nonce,\n                0,\n                address(0)\n            )\n        );\n\n        bytes32 digest = keccak256(\n            abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", entrypoint.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(), intentHash)\n        );\n\n        // Owner signs the digest\n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(ownerKey, digest);\n        \n        // Verify wallet would accept this via EIP-1271\n        bytes memory sig = abi.encodePacked(r, s, v);\n        bytes4 magic = wallet.isValidSignature(digest, sig);\n        require(magic == 0x1626ba7e, \"Wallet should validate via EIP-1271\");\n\n        // Show what ECDSA.recover returns\n        address recovered = ecrecover(digest, v, r, s);\n        \n        require(recovered == owner, \"Sanity check: ECDSA returns owner\");\n        require(recovered != address(wallet), \"POC: Owner != Wallet\");\n\n        // Attempt deposit - will fail\n        console.log(\"Attempting depositToIntent...\");\n        vm.expectRevert(TrailsIntentEntrypoint.InvalidIntentSignature.selector);\n        \n        entrypoint.depositToIntent(\n            address(wallet),\n            address(token),\n            amount,\n            intentAddr,\n            deadline,\n            nonce,\n            0,\n            address(0),\n            v,\n            r,\n            s\n        );\n    }\n    \n}\n```",
